{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the middle bar, in the midst of the boards, shall pass through from end to end.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: there were five bars for the north wall, five bars for the south, and five for the west; and these five are actually three, for the upper bar consisted of two halves, and likewise the lower bar, but the middle one was whole, its length thirty cubits, and this is ״from end to end״ — from east to west. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: it stood by miracle. But the Tosafot explained that it passed through three sides: the north wall thirty cubits, and the south wall also thirty cubits, and twelve cubits for the west — so the middle bar was seventy cubits, the two cubits being absorbed into the western end." "<b>And set</b> your heart [on this]: for the middle bar that binds the ends and girds the entire Mishkan on all sides and supports it — it corresponds to the middle line of the Holy Temple, which bears and supports all the extremities and channels its power into all the seventy supreme princes. And this is the measure of Jacob, for through his power seventy souls went forth, and if so, it was fitting for Jacob our father to bring it down to Egypt; thus they said in Midrash Tanchuma: the middle bar went down with Jacob our father to Egypt. He said to his sons: when you are redeemed, take it with you."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:46.162963765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}